  "headline": "Everything sold but the dollar: the squeeze has started and oil ignores burning tankers",
  "body": [
    "Stocks fell 1.9% today and the VIX jumped to 23, mid-range but up nearly a fifth in one session. Oil, copper and gold were sold alongside them, and the only bid was the dollar, at a new yearly high of 103.5. That is not a boom being repriced. It is a deleveraging: cash being raised, and the dollar is the cash.",
    "Last session I read stocks up 2.5% on the week against rising yields as growth plus a believed Fed; that lasted one day, and the S&P is now down 1.8% on the week. What held was staying out of gold and the long bond and not fighting the dollar. What has changed is the front end: the 5-year rallied 5 basis points today while the 30-year gave back barely 1, so the market has begun pricing a Fed leaning into weakness and a long bond refusing to follow.",
    "Gold at $3,869 is a new yearly low, and it fell on a day yields fell and the VIX rose. That is no longer orderly selling under real rates; that is gold sold to meet margin calls, the same force that took bitcoin down 13% this week. My trigger for calling it forced selling needed the dollar to fall too, and it rose 0.1%, so by the letter I stay out. But liquidation ends in a way real-rate selling does not, and a 30-year that will not rally in a 2% equity drop, with MOVE above 100, is the first fiscal-dominance tell I have seen in weeks.",
    "Drop Site's headline today has oil tankers burning in Hormuz, and Brent fell 4.7% to $91.5. A war hedge that loses nearly 5% on the day tankers burn in the strait is not a hedge, it is a growth bet in disguise, and growth is what is being sold. The rupee has firmed 0.75% against the dollar on the month, so the oil importer is not paying either. I cut Brent; the market says supply is fine and demand is not, and I have been wrong on that leg long enough.",
    "My book: out of gold, out of the 30-year, out of Brent, holding dollar cash, which is the most uncomfortable position I have held because it is the market's trade and not mine. Bitcoin up 1.3% while stocks fell is the one odd print; one day of a liquidity hedge behaving like one proves nothing, three would make me add. The way back into gold is the first close higher on a day the VIX is also higher, a haven acting like one; above $4,000 with a softer dollar confirms it. What proves the squeeze read wrong is stocks recovering with the 5-year back above 5%, the believed Fed again, and gold with further to fall. Next I watch the 30-year minus 5-year spread, 53 basis points and wider on the day: through 60 with stocks lower and the old view is back."
  ],
